From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cli: resolve wireless parent from live AP BSS owner

The container lab carries IEEE 1905 control traffic over a shared sideband L2
path.  The controller transport hierarchy can consequently remain a star even
after the Wi-Fi data plane has formed a multi-hop backhaul chain.  The topology
endpoint already exposes every child's current upstream BSSID, but copied the
stale transport-tree parent into the edge's from field.

Build a bounded ownership index from live AP BSS rows and resolve each wireless
edge through the unique owner of its upstream BSSID.  Do not use backhaul STA
rows because they repeat the upstream BSSID in every child.  Missing, ambiguous
and self-owned BSSIDs retain the controller edge rather than inventing a parent.
Also source the edge band and channel from the resolved parent AP.

This makes the API, WebUI and multihop acceptance test describe the physical
backhaul tree while leaving the controller's internal transport tree unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [HWSIM evaluation WebUI]
